 "result_text": "Private keys in the default SSH directory are now found. I haven't run the tests or any other check (flake8 isn't installed in this environment).\n\nIn `get_keys` in `sshtunnel.py`, the whole key search was wrapped in `if host_pkey_directories is not None:`. When `host_pkey_directories` was `None` (the default), the search never ran, so the `or [DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY]` fallback was unreachable. I removed that guard. Now `None` or an empty list falls back to `DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY`, and a non-empty list is searched as before.\n\nThe rest of the diff is the loop body moving one indentation level left.\n\nOne behaviour change to be aware of: callers who never set `host_pkey_directories` will now have keys in `~/.ssh` loaded where none were before. This matches the existing `# look for keys in ~/.ssh` comment on the default.",
